            <ArticleTitle>Pyomyositis of the iliacus muscle complicated with septic sacroiliitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>983-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/qjmed/hcn092</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a rare case of pyomyositis of the iliacus muscle in a 29-year-old woman. After 2 weeks of adequate treatment, secondary septic sacroiliitis occurred, a complication that had not been described previously. Pyomyositis of the iliacus muscle must be considered in the differential diagnosis of acute pain in the hip region.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
